  "starterCode": "import math\nfrom collections import Counter\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef tfidf_vectorizer(documents: list[str]) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns a dictionary with tfidf_matrix and vocabulary.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Write code here\n    pass",
  "createdAt": "2025-10-30T23:00:02.228Z",
  "updatedAt": "2026-03-05T20:47:30.374Z",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nVectorized, numerically stable reference implementation following exact specifications.\n\n### 💻 Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport math\nfrom collections import Counter\n\ndef tfidf_vectorizer(documents: list[str]) -> dict:\n    tokenized = [doc.lower().split() for doc in documents]\n    vocab = sorted(list(set(w for doc in tokenized for w in doc)))\n    N = len(documents)\n    df = Counter()\n    for doc in tokenized:\n        for w in set(doc):\n            df[w] += 1\n    matrix = []\n    for doc in tokenized:\n        counts = Counter(doc)\n        total = len(doc)\n        row = []\n        for w in vocab:\n            tf = counts[w] / total if total > 0 else 0.0\n            idf = math.log(N / df[w]) if df[w] > 0 else 0.0\n            row.append(round(tf * idf, 6))\n        matrix.append(row)\n    return {'tfidf_matrix': matrix, 'vocabulary': vocab}\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the input dimensions.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ for memory buffers.\n",
